  "venue": {
    "heading": "Getting there",
    "intro": "Nave Carolina is in Iñaquito, Quito, a short walk from La Carolina Metro station.",
    "feature": {
      "title": "Tarnell shuttle",
      "tag": "Recommended",
      "body": "Free shuttle from UIO arrivals to Nave Carolina. Mon Apr 10, 10:00 AM to 10:00 PM, every 30 minutes."
    },
    "mapLink": "",
    "items": [
      {
        "title": "Metro",
        "body": "Quito Metro Line 1 runs underground from Quitumbe in the south to El Labrador in the north, 15 stations. Get off at La Carolina station, at Avenida Eloy Alfaro and Avenida de La República, at the south end of Parque La Carolina next to the financial district. Nave Carolina is a short walk from the station."
      },
      {
        "title": "Paying for the Metro",
        "body": "Tarjeta Ciudad card, or cash at the turnstile."
      },
      {
        "title": "From the airport",
        "body": "Mariscal Sucre International (UIO) is in Tababela. The Metro doesn't reach the airport. Public buses run from the airport to the Río Coca and Carcelén terminals in the north and Quitumbe in the south, and taxis wait outside arrivals."
      },
      {
        "title": "Altitude",
        "body": "Quito sits at about 2,850 m (9,350 ft). Plan an easy first day and drink water."
      }
    ]
  },
